# The vendored W3C suites are conformance fixtures whose exact bytes are the
# test. Several hold literals whose value is a raw line feed --
# rdf11-turtle/literal_with_LINE_FEED.ttl is `'''<LF>'''`, and the subm-15/16
# cases embed newlines in """ literals. A checkout that translates those to
# CRLF changes the literal's value, so the parse is no longer isomorphic to
# the expected N-Triples: six eval tests fail on Windows without this.
tests/w3c/** -text

# Benchmark corpora are measured by bytes parsed per second; line-ending
# translation would silently change both the input and the throughput.
bench/corpus/** -text

# Odin sources are ordinary text wherever they sit, including the suite
# harness and the corpus loader inside the directories above. Last matching
# pattern wins, so this re-exempts them.
*.odin text=auto
